  "body": "All applied to the dev account today and, until now, living only in a working tree. A rebuild from a clean clone would have reproduced each failure in order.\n\n**CI role trust policy** — matched only the classic OIDC subject. GitHub issues an immutable form for this repo (`repo:owner@136675538/name@1355406331:...`), so STS refused with `Not authorized to perform sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity` against a policy correct in every visible field. Both forms now accepted; wildcards cover only the ID suffixes.\n\n**ECR policy** — had the six write actions and no reads. buildx resolves the existing manifest before uploading, so the push failed after build and scan both passed. `BatchGetImage` + `DescribeImages` added, scoped to the same repository ARNs; cosign needs them too.\n\n**Kyverno IRSA** — Kyverno had no AWS identity, so it couldn't fetch the cosign signature from private ECR. Admission timed out rather than reporting an auth failure, making a correctly signed image look unsigned. Read-only, not scoped to one repo since Kyverno reads whatever it verifies.\n\n**`system_node_instance_types` → t3.large** — t3.medium caps at 17 pods/node and three filled entirely, leaving ArgoCD unschedulable and stalling a helm upgrade.\n\n⚠️ The instance type change **replaces the node group** (destroy-then-create). ArgoCD and Karpenter are both pinned to it — expect an outage window, and have the Kyverno webhook teardown step ready in case admission deadlocks.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
